# The sdist ships the package and not the test suite, on purpose.
#
# The suite tests this REPOSITORY, not just the installable package: nearly every module reads
# examples/, config/, tools/, .github/, README.md or CLAUDE.md, or imports the HR simulator
# (src/askback_sim). Measured: with every test file included, the extracted sdist fails at
# collection (a missing config file) before a single test runs. Making it runnable would mean
# shipping the simulator, the examples and CI files in the sdist as well, which contradicts
# keeping the simulator out of what we publish. setuptools would otherwise pick up only
# `tests/test*.py` and drop conftest.py and expected_tests.json: a suite that looks present and
# cannot run is worse than one that is absent. Run the tests from a clone.
#
# The release workflow fails the build if a tests/ path appears in the sdist.
prune tests
global-exclude __pycache__ *.py[cod]
